{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROOT CAUSE CORRECTED (supersedes the outbound-churn framing). Traced the full seam:\n\nOUTBOUND is NOT the exposed direction. diff_canonical_fields->_suppressed_by_inbound (outbound_field_diff.py:330) suppresses a mirrored field whenever local==baseline. After our own push the baseline advances to NEW (e6e9 merge_baseline overlay via synced_fields), so local(NEW)==baseline(NEW) -> outbound emits NOTHING for description regardless of the stale snapshot. Outbound cannot churn here.\n\nThe EXPOSED direction is INBOUND, LEVEL-triggered with NO baseline. Bound-field inbound goes through inbound_differ.compute_inbound_mutations -> _diff_jira_vs_local(jira_fields, local) (inbound_differ.py:97), returning any mirrored field where the CURRENT snapshot != local, consulting neither baseline nor prev_snapshot. run_differs._run_differs_inbound feeds it curr_snapshot (the JQL search snapshot) plus only an absent-key GET overlay -- no prev gating. The only protection is same-pass bidirectional suppression (3bf8), which fires only when OUTBOUND emits for the field. Since outbound is baseline-suppressed here, inbound is unguarded.\n\nConsequence (narrow but real data-loss window): in the echo pass with a STALE post-write snapshot (description=OLD/None) while local=NEW and baseline=NEW, inbound sees jira(OLD)!=local(NEW) -> emits an inbound update -> CLOBBERS local back to OLD. The live test's _wait_until_search_reflects is a DEFENSIVE wait blocking the echo pass until the search index reflects the write (so jira==local, nothing mirrors). On the starved ephemeral DC the background reindex is unbounded -> the wait never completes -> observed 'index never reflected the pushed body within 240s' timeout. A remote!=baseline guard would NOT fix it (baseline=NEW while stale search=OLD, so OLD!=NEW still fires); the only robust fix is a lag-free read.\n\nRESOLUTION (refined #1, correct layer): a SCOPED-pass snapshot overlay. Between bind_operation_runtime and run_differs in reconcile.reconcile_once, for each scoped local_id whose bound jira_key is present in curr_snapshot, direct-GET fresh fields via the classified seam (outbound_differ._safe_get_issue / get_issue_by_rest, immediately consistent) and MERGE the 5 mirrored scalar keys (summary/description/priority/status/assignee) into curr_snapshot[jira_key], preserving enrichment (parent/comment/issuelinks). This one overlay feeds BOTH differs AND _advance_baselines (all read ctx.curr_snapshot), so the echo pass sees jira==local -> no inbound clobber, outbound stays suppressed, baseline stays NEW. Scoped-only bounds GET volume; TRANSPORT_ERROR/DELETED leave the entry untouched (defer/existing path). Unscoped production passes get a follow-up (ambiguous-key generalization). With this, BOTH live DC tests drop _wait_until_search_reflects and the reindex entirely and read lag-free. Proven offline by a held-out oracle: stale search + fresh GET -> zero inbound clobber + baseline stays NEW (RED without the overlay: inbound emits description=OLD)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787827649930053001,"uuid":"84fcd16d-a50d-4d9a-9483-690c4d7f9b29"}